    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (global sequence) to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (per-city sequence) in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n- **`nextCustomerCode`** (`src/main/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:154`): now takes the `city` in addition to `lastName`. It prepends `CITY3` (upper-cased first three letters of the city), keeps `LAST3` (upper-cased first three of the last name), and computes `NNNN` as a **per-city** 4-digit sequence \u2014 one more than the count of existing owners already in that city (matched case-insensitively), instead of the previous global owner count.\n- Updated the call site (`:310`) to pass `owner.getCity()`.\n\n**Derived values rebuild automatically:** the membership number in `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber(...)` is built as `getCustomerCode() + \"-M<YY>\"`, so it now uses the new `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` base without any change there \u2014 e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, which asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`, passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
